{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You send a message. The UI sits still until the model is done. That wait feels broken."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stream the reply. Tokens show up as the model writes them."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-send-the-stream-from-the-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Send the stream from the server"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":". Then wrap the result with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toServerSentEventsResponse"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n    messages,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatParamsFromRequest"},{"type":"text","value":" reads the AG-UI body that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" sends. If the body is invalid, it throws a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response"},{"type":"text","value":" with status 400. If your framework does not map a thrown "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response"},{"type":"text","value":" to HTTP 400, catch it and return it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The response stream pauses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" when its output queue is full. It reads more chunks when the client consumes the queued data. This also applies to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toHttpResponse"},{"type":"text","value":" with NDJSON. A response with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"durability"},{"type":"text","value":" does not pause, so its run keeps writing to the log."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-render-with-usechat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Render with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n            part.type === \"text\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\n          )}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault();\n          if (input.trim() === \"\") {\n            return;\n          }\n          sendMessage(input);\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input\n          value={input}\n          onChange={(event) => setInput(event.target.value)}\n        />\n        {isLoading ? (\n          <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n            Stop\n          </button>\n        ) : (\n          <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n        )}\n      </form>\n    </>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" updates as chunks arrive. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isLoading"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" while the run is in flight."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The shared "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatClient"},{"type":"text","value":" processes ready chunks in order without inserting a task between each chunk. It yields after bounded processing work to keep the main thread responsive."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same pattern works in every UI framework. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../getting-started/quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If SSE is blocked, pick another transport on "},{"type":"link","href":"../transports/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transports"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-cancel-a-run","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Cancel a run"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":". The client aborts the fetch."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AbortController"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toServerSentEventsResponse"},{"type":"text","value":" so the server stops the model too:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const abortController = new AbortController();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n    messages,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n    abortController,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream, { abortController });\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AbortError"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":" is expected. Pending client-tool work for that turn does not resume. A later "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"addToolResult()"},{"type":"text","value":" for that turn is ignored."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A dropped connection mid-line throws "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamTruncatedError"},{"type":"text","value":". The client then moves to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"../transports/overview#errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transports: Errors"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For OpenAI and OpenRouter Responses, a stream that ends without "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"response.completed"},{"type":"text","value":" emits "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_ERROR"},{"type":"text","value":" with code "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"incomplete-stream"},{"type":"text","value":". This applies to chat and to structured output. Text received before the error remains available. The run does not call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFinish"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat Completions adapters built on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/openai-base"},{"type":"text","value":" also check completion in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":". A started stream needs a non-null "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finish_reason"},{"type":"text","value":" or a final usage-only chunk ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"choices: []"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usage"},{"type":"text","value":"). Otherwise, the adapter closes open lifecycles and emits "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_ERROR"},{"type":"text","value":" with code "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"incomplete-stream"},{"type":"text","value":". Partial text remains available. The run calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"},{"type":"text","value":", skips pending server tools, and does not call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFinish"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The usage-only exception preserves provider compatibility. Usage on an earlier chunk or alongside a choice does not satisfy it. The OpenAI SDK hides "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[DONE]"},{"type":"text","value":", so this check cannot verify that marker. A stream with only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[DONE]"},{"type":"text","value":" after content still needs a finish reason or usage-only tail to succeed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"later","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Later"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No HTTP."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Iterate "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" yourself. Branch on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.type === \"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\""},{"type":"text","value":". Then read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.delta"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callbacks."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" fires on each event. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFinish"},{"type":"text","value":" fires with the completed message."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Send while a reply is in flight."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Messages wait in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queue"},{"type":"text","value":" by default. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./queueing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Message Queue"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Event types, thread ids, and tool parts."}]},{"type":"text","value":" See "},{"type":"link","href":"./stream-events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stream Events"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Thinking tokens or a refresh mid-stream."}]},{"type":"text","value":" See "},{"type":"link","href":"./thinking-content","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Thinking and Reasoning"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"../resumable-streams/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resumable Streams"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Send a message. Text grows in the UI as tokens arrive."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"1-send-the-stream-from-the-server","text":"1. Send the stream from the server","level":2},{"id":"2-render-with-usechat","text":"2. Render with useChat","level":2},{"id":"3-cancel-a-run","text":"3. Cancel a run","level":2},{"id":"later","text":"Later","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou send a message. The UI sits still until the model is done. That wait feels broken.\n\nStream the reply. Tokens show up as the model writes them.\n\n## 1. Send the stream from the server\n\nCall `chat()`. Then wrap the result with `toServerSentEventsResponse`:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n    messages,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n`chatParamsFromRequest` reads the AG-UI body that `useChat` sends. If the body is invalid, it throws a `Response` with status 400. If your framework does not map a thrown `Response` to HTTP 400, catch it and return it.\n\nThe response stream pauses `chat()` when its output queue is full. It reads more chunks when the client consumes the queued data. This also applies to `toHttpResponse` with NDJSON. A response with `durability` does not pause, so its run keeps writing to the log.\n\n## 2. Render with `useChat`\n\n```tsx\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n            part.type === \"text\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\n          )}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault();\n          if (input.trim() === \"\") {\n            return;\n          }\n          sendMessage(input);\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input\n          value={input}\n          onChange={(event) => setInput(event.target.value)}\n        />\n        {isLoading ? (\n          <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n            Stop\n          </button>\n        ) : (\n          <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n        )}\n      </form>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n`messages` updates as chunks arrive. `isLoading` is `true` while the run is in flight.\n\nThe shared `ChatClient` processes ready chunks in order without inserting a task between each chunk. It yields after bounded processing work to keep the main thread responsive.\n\nThe same pattern works in every UI framework. See [Quick Start](../getting-started/quick-start).\n\nIf SSE is blocked, pick another transport on [Transports](../transports/overview).\n\n## 3. Cancel a run\n\nCall `stop()`. The client aborts the fetch.\n\nPass the same `AbortController` to `chat()` and `toServerSentEventsResponse` so the server stops the model too:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const abortController = new AbortController();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n    messages,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n    abortController,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream, { abortController });\n}\n```\n\n`AbortError` from `stop()` is expected. Pending client-tool work for that turn does not resume. A later `addToolResult()` for that turn is ignored.\n\nA dropped connection mid-line throws `StreamTruncatedError`. The client then moves to `error`. See [Transports: Errors](../transports/overview#errors).\n\nFor OpenAI and OpenRouter Responses, a stream that ends without `response.completed` emits `RUN_ERROR` with code `incomplete-stream`. This applies to chat and to structured output. Text received before the error remains available. The run does not call `onFinish`.\n\nChat Completions adapters built on `@tanstack/openai-base` also check completion in `chat()`. A started stream needs a non-null `finish_reason` or a final usage-only chunk (`choices: []` with `usage`). Otherwise, the adapter closes open lifecycles and emits `RUN_ERROR` with code `incomplete-stream`. Partial text remains available. The run calls `onError`, skips pending server tools, and does not call `onFinish`.\n\nThe usage-only exception preserves provider compatibility. Usage on an earlier chunk or alongside a choice does not satisfy it. The OpenAI SDK hides `[DONE]`, so this check cannot verify that marker. A stream with only `[DONE]` after content still needs a finish reason or usage-only tail to succeed.\n\n## Later\n\n- **No HTTP.** Iterate `chat()` yourself. Branch on `chunk.type === \"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\"`. Then read `chunk.delta`.\n- **Callbacks.** `onChunk` fires on each event. `onFinish` fires with the completed message.\n- **Send while a reply is in flight.** Messages wait in `queue` by default. See [Message Queue](./queueing).\n- **Event types, thread ids, and tool parts.** See [Stream Events](./stream-events).\n- **Thinking tokens or a refresh mid-stream.** See [Thinking and Reasoning](./thinking-content) and [Resumable Streams](../resumable-streams/overview).\n\nSend a message. Text grows in the UI as tokens arrive.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Streaming\nid: streaming-responses\norder: 2\ndescription: \"Show AI tokens in the UI as they arrive. Server stream, client useChat, cancel, and callbacks.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - streaming\n  - streaming responses\n  - real-time ai\n  - async iterable\n  - chunks\n  - useChat\n---\n\nYou send a message. The UI sits still until the model is done. That wait feels broken.\n\nStream the reply. Tokens show up as the model writes them.\n\n## 1. Send the stream from the server\n\nCall `chat()`. Then wrap the result with `toServerSentEventsResponse`:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n    messages,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n`chatParamsFromRequest` reads the AG-UI body that `useChat` sends. If the body is invalid, it throws a `Response` with status 400. If your framework does not map a thrown `Response` to HTTP 400, catch it and return it.\n\nThe response stream pauses `chat()` when its output queue is full. It reads more chunks when the client consumes the queued data. This also applies to `toHttpResponse` with NDJSON. A response with `durability` does not pause, so its run keeps writing to the log.\n\n## 2. Render with `useChat`\n\n```tsx\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n            part.type === \"text\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\n          )}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault();\n          if (input.trim() === \"\") {\n            return;\n          }\n          sendMessage(input);\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input\n          value={input}\n          onChange={(event) => setInput(event.target.value)}\n        />\n        {isLoading ? (\n          <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n            Stop\n          </button>\n        ) : (\n          <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n        )}\n      </form>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n`messages` updates as chunks arrive. `isLoading` is `true` while the run is in flight.\n\nThe shared `ChatClient` processes ready chunks in order without inserting a task between each chunk. It yields after bounded processing work to keep the main thread responsive.\n\nThe same pattern works in every UI framework. See [Quick Start](../getting-started/quick-start).\n\nIf SSE is blocked, pick another transport on [Transports](../transports/overview).\n\n## 3. Cancel a run\n\nCall `stop()`. The client aborts the fetch.\n\nPass the same `AbortController` to `chat()` and `toServerSentEventsResponse` so the server stops the model too:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const abortController = new AbortController();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n    messages,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n    abortController,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream, { abortController });\n}\n```\n\n`AbortError` from `stop()` is expected. Pending client-tool work for that turn does not resume. A later `addToolResult()` for that turn is ignored.\n\nA dropped connection mid-line throws `StreamTruncatedError`. The client then moves to `error`. See [Transports: Errors](../transports/overview#errors).\n\nFor OpenAI and OpenRouter Responses, a stream that ends without `response.completed` emits `RUN_ERROR` with code `incomplete-stream`. This applies to chat and to structured output. Text received before the error remains available. The run does not call `onFinish`.\n\nChat Completions adapters built on `@tanstack/openai-base` also check completion in `chat()`. A started stream needs a non-null `finish_reason` or a final usage-only chunk (`choices: []` with `usage`). Otherwise, the adapter closes open lifecycles and emits `RUN_ERROR` with code `incomplete-stream`. Partial text remains available. The run calls `onError`, skips pending server tools, and does not call `onFinish`.\n\nThe usage-only exception preserves provider compatibility. Usage on an earlier chunk or alongside a choice does not satisfy it. The OpenAI SDK hides `[DONE]`, so this check cannot verify that marker. A stream with only `[DONE]` after content still needs a finish reason or usage-only tail to succeed.\n\n## Later\n\n- **No HTTP.** Iterate `chat()` yourself. Branch on `chunk.type === \"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\"`. Then read `chunk.delta`.\n- **Callbacks.** `onChunk` fires on each event. `onFinish` fires with the completed message.\n- **Send while a reply is in flight.** Messages wait in `queue` by default. See [Message Queue](./queueing).\n- **Event types, thread ids, and tool parts.** See [Stream Events](./stream-events).\n- **Thinking tokens or a refresh mid-stream.** See [Thinking and Reasoning](./thinking-content) and [Resumable Streams](../resumable-streams/overview).\n\nSend a message. Text grows in the UI as tokens arrive.\n"}
